:: Sister studying_college [interaction] {"position":"525,2350","size":"100,100"}
/* Talk scene ("Chat with her", Define Interactions): $sister studying at college. She has no time for me here, so
   these are short and change nothing. */
<<silently>>
<<set _pick to setup.pickTalkScene("Sister studying_college", [1, 2, 3])>>
<</silently>>
<<DisplayActivity $sister 500>>
<<switch _pick>>

/* ——— 1: The note ——— */
<<case 1>>
I find her at a corner table in the library, behind a wall of textbooks and a bag of gummy bears. She has her big headphones on. When I sit down across from her, she looks up, takes in who it is, and holds up one finger without taking the headphones off.

She tears a corner off her notes, writes something on it and slides it over.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ text: "EXAM TOMORROW. I AM A HOLLOW SHELL. GO AWAY. ♥" },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

Under that, smaller: 'take a gummy bear on your way out, the red ones are mine'. I take a green one. She watches me do it and nods, very seriously, like we've just completed a deal, and goes back to her book.

/* ——— 2: The study group ——— */
<<case 2>>
She's at one of the big tables in the student lounge with two classmates, a guy in a baseball cap and a girl with a highlighter in each hand, and the table between them is mostly flashcards and coffee cups. She spots me and waves, and then remembers she's in public and turns it into something more casual.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "Guys, this is $player.name, my little $sister.callPlayerShort. He runs a company, so be nice to him and maybe he'll hire you someday. Probably not, though." },
{ text: "The guy in the cap says 'hey, man'. The girl with the highlighters looks me up and down with open interest, and $sister.callName notices that and moves her coffee cup about an inch to the left, into the girl's line of sight." },
{ who: $sister, text: "So what's up? We have about forty minutes left to learn an entire semester." },
{ who: $player, text: "Nothing, I was just passing by." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Great, love that. See you at home!" },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

It's not quite rude. It's quick, and it's cheerful, and it has a closing door at the end of it. She's already turned back to the flashcards before I'm out of earshot, but when I look back from the door, she's watching me go.

/* ——— 3: Calc ——— */
<<case 3>>
She's sitting on the floor in the hallway, back against the wall and legs stretched out, with a calculus book open on her knees and a pencil behind each ear. She's muttering at the page.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "Don't talk to me. If I stop now, the chain rule falls out of my head and I'll have to start all over." },
{ who: $player, text: "$prof.callName's class?" },
{ who: $sister, text: "Who else's? He gave us a 'small' problem set of thirty problems, and I'm not exaggerating, $sister.callPlayer, he made the little air quotes himself, with his own hands." },
{ text: "She writes something, crosses it out and writes it again, harder." },
{ who: $sister, text: "I have to go. I mean, you have to go, I'm staying right here. Love you, bye." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

I leave her to it. She'll pass, of course. She passed last time too, and she still thinks that was all her.

<</switch>>

<div class="navigation-link"><<link "Leave her to her studies" $player.location.passage>><</link>></div>
